{
  "id": "q-81695",
  "parts": [
    {
      "part": "problem",
      "original_record": "before",
      "value": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/assets/3b539190899ca580528fdbf7b5d3ef9925ade29f97f4b2f96b0f1394743f40a8.png)\n\nGiven the sets $S=\\{p,a,s,w,o,r,d\\}$ and $T=\\{p,o,r,t,e,l\\},$ find $T∖S.$",
      "original_html_sha256": "bbf9ec6e6955dae02c767802f7265b245357de43b18d29b0a78485831cefb75d",
      "extractor_sha256": "1591183da328a4140792793d2cc113fd535ab5f25bc7f284ceb1b6f251efad18",
      "source_file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/repairs/source-provenance-v2/structured-source/source/bbf9ec6e6955dae02c767802f7265b245357de43b18d29b0a78485831cefb75d.html",
      "extraction_errors": []
    },
    {
      "part": "worked_solution",
      "original_record": "history",
      "value": "The difference $T∖S$ consists of all the elements that are in $T$ but not $S.$ To represent $T∖S,$ we will shade in all the area that is contained in $T$ but not $S.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071857/assets/c718918667c5076f8696ea98f453ff17f005d5f7cace87bd863be309fac28d72.png)\n\nThe elements $t,e,$ and $l$ are in $T$ but not $S.$\n\nTherefore, the difference is\n\n$$\nT∖S=\\{t,e,l\\}.\n$$",
      "original_html_sha256": "ea2970e8244892418f424755890805f746830095c9690cead1189195116aea6c",
      "extractor_sha256": "1591183da328a4140792793d2cc113fd535ab5f25bc7f284ceb1b6f251efad18",
